      "sourceTextSha256": "ec105cea3e94aee7ff805c67ac26beee5ecf53221d2a2919991eba200b7fe303",
      "text": "Flight to Recife; meeting on arrival and transfer to the hotel. Time to rest. The capital of Pernambuco lies at the mouth of the Capibaribe River on the Atlantic, and is called the “Brazilian Venice” for its many canals and bridges. Despite its rapid growth, the city has kept traces of Portuguese and Dutch rule, with magnificent churches and historic mansions, beautiful beaches nearby, and many cafés, restaurants, shops and a lively nightlife.",
